\newlabel{fig:h1-frontier}{{4}{20}{\textbf {Canonical frontier batch on the one-packet basis.} The one-packet H1 run never improves the seed best objective, even though some terminal restarts lower $\ell _1$ and maximum defect after increasing support far above the seed support $13$. Greedy and simulated annealing stay pinned to the seed. This is the negative control that motivates the retained-basis redesign.\relax }{figure.caption.24}{}}
